{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 31,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.089,
            0.589,
            0.139
          ],
          "content": "Simplify $\\frac { 1 0 ^ { 4 } } { 5 ^ { 4 } }$ and write it in exponential form. **Ans:** $2 ^ { 4 }   = 1 6$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.161,
            0.276,
            0.181
          ],
          "content": "**Page No. 26**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.188,
            0.846,
            0.255
          ],
          "content": "? Roxie has 7 dresses, 2 hats, and 3 pairs of shoes. How many different ways can Roxie dress up? **Ans:** $7 \\times 2 \\times 3$ ways"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.276,
            0.275,
            0.295
          ],
          "content": "**Page No. 27**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.302,
            0.662,
            0.351
          ],
          "content": "How many passwords are possible with such a lock? **Ans:** $2 6 \\times 2 6 \\times 2 6 \\times 2 6 \\times 2 6 \\times 2 6 = ( 2 6 ) ^ { 6 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.359,
            0.467,
            0.449
          ],
          "content": "？ What is $2 ^ { 1 0 0 } \\div 2 ^ { 2 5 }$ in powers of 2? **Ans:** $2 ^ { 7 5 }$ **Page No. 28**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.455,
            0.622,
            0.504
          ],
          "content": "Why can’t n be 0? **Ans:** If $n = 0 _ { j }$ , then we get $\\frac { 0 } { 0 }$ which is not defined."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.523,
            0.275,
            0.543
          ],
          "content": "**Page No. 29**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.551,
            0.845,
            0.616
          ],
          "content": "？ We had required a and b to be counting numbers. Can a and b be any integers? Will the generalised forms still hold true? **Ans:** Yes."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.623,
            0.74,
            0.688
          ],
          "content": "？ Write equivalent forms of the following. (i) $2 ^ { - 4 }$ (ii) $1 0 ^ { - 5 }$ (iii) $( - 7 ) ^ { - 2 }$ (iv) $( - 5 ) ^ { -   3 }$ (v) $1 0 ^ { - 1 0 0 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.692,
            0.73,
            0.776
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:** (i) $\\frac { 1 } { 2 ^ { 4 } }$ (ii) $\\frac { 1 } { 1 0 ^ { 5 } }$ (iii) $\\frac { 1 } { ( - 7 ) ^ { 2 } }$ (iv) $\\frac{1^{\\circ}}{(-5)^{3}}$ (v) $\\frac{1}{(10)^{100}}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.781,
            0.758,
            0.845
          ],
          "content": "？ Simplify and write the answers in exponential form. (i) $2 ^ { - 4 } \\times 2 ^ { 7 }$ (ii) $3 ^ { 2 } \\times 3 ^ { - 5 } \\times 3 ^ { 6 }$ (iii) $p ^ { 3 } \\times p ^ { - 1 0 }$ (iv) $2 ^ { 4 }   \\times \\left( - 4 \\right) ^ { - 2 }$ (v) $8 ^ { p } \\times 8 ^ { q }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.85,
            0.718,
            0.906
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:** (i) $2 ^ { 3 }$ (ii) $3 ^ { 3 }$ (iii) $p ^ { - 7 }$ (iv) $1$ (v) $8 ^ { p + q }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.859,
